Key things to watch:
1. Put your equations in separate equations blocks (one per equation)
2. Use uppercase letters for variables/symbols
3. Place equation environments around the equations (like $\begin{eqnarray}, \end{eqnarray}$)
4. Wrap text in backticks for TeX markup
5. Mention main physics topics with their standard numbering (1.1, 1.2, etc.)

